       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and some guidelines cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose that high risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function. A single 3,000 mg dose also exceeds the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want the original dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still be reluctant to enter it without a pharmacist's or attending's review."
      }
